        money: "Net debt of about ₹56cr on Screener; the company puts debt at just 0.07 times equity after its August 2025 IPO, which helped cut borrowings from ₹509cr to ₹256cr. Capex rose to ₹136cr in FY26 and will continue as capacity doubles. Operating cash flow is thin (₹13cr in FY26) because stock and receivables grow with sales. In September 2026 it raised about ₹1,500cr by placing new shares with institutions at ₹3,467, about 6% below the market price (43.26 lakh new shares: 3.7% more shares, which cuts existing holders' stake by 3.5%), for debt repayment, capex and possible acquisitions. Customs demands of ₹39cr (mainly on imported routers) and GST demands of ₹35cr are under appeal. Promoters hold **74.7%**, down from 77.1% in September 2025, and the placement lowers that further.",
        watch: ["Operating cash turning clearly positive in H1 FY27, after ₹13cr in FY26.", "Whether the roughly 25% price rises stick without losing buyers.", "Margin holding in the guided 14-15% range as memory costs rise.", "Any change to the rule barring Chinese chips from CCTV."],
